{"id":"mahabharata-3-049","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":49,"title":"एकोनपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 49 · Brihadashva comes; Yudhishthira's lament","summary":{"en":"The Pandavas grieve for the absent Arjuna and Bhima chafes at the delay. The sage Brihadashva arrives, and Yudhishthira asks whether any king was ever more unfortunate than he; Brihadashva promises the story of King Nala, who suffered more.","kn":"ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಲ್ಲದೆ ಪಾಂಡವರು ದುಃಖಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಭೀಮನು ತಡದಿಂದ ಅಸಹನೆಗೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಬೃಹದಶ್ವ ಋಷಿ ಬಂದಾಗ ತನಗಿಂತ ದುರದೃಷ್ಟ ರಾಜನು ಇದ್ದನೇ ಎಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಇನ್ನೂ ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಕಷ್ಟಪಟ್ಟ ನಳರಾಜನ ಕಥೆ ಹೇಳುವೆನೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"अनुपस्थित अर्जुन के लिए पाण्डव शोक करते हैं और भीम विलम्ब से अधीर होते हैं। ऋषि बृहदश्व आते हैं, और युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि क्या कोई राजा उनसे अधिक अभागा हुआ है; बृहदश्व राजा नल की कथा सुनाने का वचन देते हैं, जिन्होंने अधिक कष्ट सहे।","te":"అర్జునుడు లేక పాండవులు దుఃఖిస్తారు, భీముడు ఆలస్యానికి అసహనపడతాడు. బృహదశ్వ మహర్షి రాగా తనకంటే దురదృష్టవంతుడైన రాజు ఎవరైనా ఉన్నాడా అని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; ఇంకా ఎక్కువ కష్టాలు పడిన నలమహారాజు కథ చెబుతానంటాడు.","ta":"அர்ஜுனன் இல்லாததால் பாண்டவர்கள் வருந்த, பீமன் தாமதத்தால் பொறுமையிழக்கிறான். ப்ருஹதஶ்வ முனிவர் வர, தம்மைவிட துரதிர்ஷ்டமான மன்னன் எவனாவது உண்டா என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்கிறார்; இன்னும் அதிகம் துன்புற்ற நள மன்னனின் கதையைச் சொல்வதாக அவர் வாக்களிக்கிறார்.","ml":"വരാതിരിക്കുന്ന അർജുനനെയോർത്ത് പാണ്ഡവർ ദുഃഖിക്കുന്നു; കാലതാമസത്തിൽ ഭീമൻ അസ്വസ്ഥനാകുന്നു. ബൃഹദശ്വൻ മുനി എത്തുന്നു; ഇതിലും ദുർഭാഗ്യവാനായ ഒരു രാജാവുണ്ടോ എന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; അതിലും കൂടുതൽ കഷ്ടപ്പെട്ട നളരാജാവിന്റെ കഥ പറയാമെന്ന് ബൃഹദശ്വൻ വാക്കു നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.49; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"इन्द्रलोकाभिगमनपर्व","titleEn":"Indralokabhigamana Parva (Journey to Indra's world)","verses":[{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अस्त्रहेतोर्गते पार्थे शक्रलोकं महात्मनि ।\nयुधिष्ठिरप्रभृतयः किमकुर्वन्त पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Partha, the great soul, went to Indra's world for weapons, what did Yudhishthira and the other Pandavas do?"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"अस्त्रहेतोर्गते पार्थे शक्रलोकं महात्मनि ।\nन्यवसन्कृष्णया सार्धं काम्यके पुरुषर्षभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After Partha went to the world of Shakra for weapons, those bulls among men lived in Kamyaka with Krishna."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततः कदाचिदेकान्ते विविक्त इव शाद्वले ।\nदुःखार्ता भरतश्रेष्ठा निषेदुः सह कृष्णया ।\nधनंजयं शोचमानाः साश्रुकण्ठाः सुदुःखिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then once, in a secluded grassy spot, the best of the Bharatas sat with Krishna, pained and sorrowful, grieving for Dhananjaya with tears in their throats."}},{"n":4,"text":"तद्वियोगाद्धि तान्सर्वाञ्शोकः समभिपुप्लुवे ।\nधनंजयवियोगाच्च राज्यनाशाच्च दुःखिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grief flooded all of them because of that separation; they were afflicted by Dhananjaya's absence and by the loss of their kingdom."}},{"n":5,"text":"अथ भीमो महाबाहुर्युधिष्ठिरमभाषत ।\nनिदेशात्ते महाराज गतोऽसौ पुरुषर्षभः ।\nअर्जुनः पाण्डुपुत्राणां यस्मिन्प्राणाः प्रतिष्ठिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then mighty-armed Bhima spoke to Yudhishthira: \"Great king, that bull among men has gone at your command, Arjuna, in whom the lives of the Pandavas rest."}},{"n":6,"text":"यस्मिन्विनष्टे पाञ्चालाः सह पुत्रैस्तथा वयम् ।\nसात्यकिर्वासुदेवश्च विनश्येयुरसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If he were lost, the Panchalas with their sons, and we, Satyaki and Vasudeva would surely be lost too."}},{"n":7,"text":"योऽसौ गच्छति तेजस्वी बहून्क्लेशानचिन्तयन् ।\nभवन्नियोगाद्बीभत्सुस्ततो दुःखतरं नु किम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That brilliant one goes, heeding many hardships, at your command. What could be sadder than this, for Bibhatsu?"}},{"n":8,"text":"यस्य बाहू समाश्रित्य वयं सर्वे महात्मनः ।\nमन्यामहे जितानाजौ परान्प्राप्तां च मेदिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Relying on whose arms we all, great-souled ones, count our enemies already beaten in battle and the earth already won,"}},{"n":9,"text":"यस्य प्रभावान्न मया सभामध्ये धनुष्मतः ।\nनीता लोकममुं सर्वे धार्तराष्ट्राः ससौबलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"by whose power I did not send all the Dhartarashtras with Saubala to the next world in the middle of the assembly, that archer is gone."}},{"n":10,"text":"ते वयं बाहुबलिनः क्रोधमुत्थितमात्मनः ।\nसहामहे भवन्मूलं वासुदेवेन पालिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We are strong-armed men, yet we bear our rising anger, rooted in you, protected by Vasudeva."}},{"n":11,"text":"वयं हि सह कृष्णेन हत्वा कर्णमुखान्परान् ।\nस्वबाहुविजितां कृत्स्नां प्रशासेम वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With Krishna we could kill Karna and the other foes and rule the whole earth won by our own arms."}},{"n":12,"text":"भवतो द्यूतदोषेण सर्वे वयमुपप्लुताः ।\nअहीनपौरुषा राजन्बलिभिर्बलवत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through your fault at dice we have all been overwhelmed, we who lack no manhood, king, and are stronger than the strong."}},{"n":13,"text":"क्षात्रं धर्मं महाराज समवेक्षितुमर्हसि ।\nन हि धर्मो महाराज क्षत्रियस्य वनाश्रयः ।\nराज्यमेव परं धर्मं क्षत्रियस्य विदुर्बुधाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, you should regard the kshatriya dharma. The forest is not a kshatriya's dharma; the wise know that a kingdom is the highest dharma of a kshatriya."}},{"n":14,"text":"स क्षत्रधर्मविद्राजन्मा धर्म्यान्नीनशः पथः ।\nप्राग्द्वादश समा राजन्धार्तराष्ट्रान्निहन्महि ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, knowing the kshatriya's duty, do not stray from the path of dharma. Let us kill the Dhartarashtras before the twelve years are up."}},{"n":15,"text":"निवर्त्य च वनात्पार्थमानाय्य च जनार्दनम् ।\nव्यूढानीकान्महाराज जवेनैव महाहवे ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रानमुं लोकं गमयामि विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Recalling Partha from the forest and bringing Janardana, lord of the people, I will send the Dhartarashtras to the next world swiftly in the great battle, even with their armies drawn up."}},{"n":16,"text":"सर्वानहं हनिष्यामि धार्तराष्ट्रान्ससौबलान् ।\nदुर्योधनं च कर्णं च यो वान्यः प्रतियोत्स्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will kill all the Dhartarashtras with Saubala, Duryodhana, Karna and whoever else fights us."}},{"n":17,"text":"मया प्रशमिते पश्चात्त्वमेष्यसि वनात्पुनः ।\nएवं कृते न ते दोषो भविष्यति विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I have calmed things, you can return to the forest again. If this is done, king, you will incur no fault."}},{"n":18,"text":"यज्ञैश्च विविधैस्तात कृतं पापमरिंदम ।\nअवधूय महाराज गच्छेम स्वर्गमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With various sacrifices, dear brother, scourge of foes, we can shake off whatever sin was done and go to the highest heaven."}},{"n":19,"text":"एवमेतद्भवेद्राजन्यदि राजा न बालिशः ।\nअस्माकं दीर्घसूत्रः स्याद्भवान्धर्मपरायणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This would be so, king, if you were not simple and slow to act, devoted only to dharma, for us."}},{"n":20,"text":"निकृत्या निकृतिप्रज्ञा हन्तव्या इति निश्चयः ।\nन हि नैकृतिकं हत्वा निकृत्या पापमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is settled that the deceitful, who think in deceit, should be killed by deceit; one who kills a cheat by cheating does not take sin."}},{"n":21,"text":"तथा भारत धर्मेषु धर्मज्ञैरिह दृश्यते ।\nअहोरात्रं महाराज तुल्यं संवत्सरेण हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too, Bharata, those who know dharma see in the dharma texts that a day and a night are equal to a year."}},{"n":22,"text":"तथैव वेदवचनं श्रूयते नित्यदा विभो ।\nसंवत्सरो महाराज पूर्णो भवति कृच्छ्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And likewise the Vedic word is always heard, lord: a year is hard to make complete."}},{"n":23,"text":"यदि वेदाः प्रमाणं ते दिवसादूर्ध्वमच्युत ।\nत्रयोदश समाः कालो ज्ञायतां परिनिष्ठितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If the Vedas are your authority, Achyuta, let the thirteen years be taken as complete after a single day."}},{"n":24,"text":"कालो दुर्योधनं हन्तुं सानुबन्धमरिंदम ।\nएकाग्रां पृथिवीं सर्वां पुरा राजन्करोति सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The time to kill Duryodhana with his followers has come, scourge of foes. He will soon unite the whole earth under him."}},{"n":25,"text":"एवं ब्रुवाणं भीमं तु धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nउवाच सान्त्वयन्राजा मूर्ध्न्युपाघ्राय पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Bhima spoke thus, Yudhishthira the king of dharma comforted him, kissing the Pandava's head."}},{"n":26,"text":"असंशयं महाबाहो हनिष्यसि सुयोधनम् ।\nवर्षात्त्रयोदशादूर्ध्वं सह गाण्डीवधन्वना ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Without doubt, mighty-armed one, you will kill Suyodhana after the thirteenth year, with the wielder of the Gandiva."}},{"n":27,"text":"यच्च मा भाषसे पार्थ प्राप्तः काल इति प्रभो ।\nअनृतं नोत्सहे वक्तुं न ह्येतन्मयि विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"But you say, Partha, that the time has come; I cannot say what is untrue, and this is not in me."}},{"n":28,"text":"अन्तरेणापि कौन्तेय निकृतिं पापनिश्चयम् ।\nहन्ता त्वमसि दुर्धर्ष सानुबन्धं सुयोधनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even without deceit and wicked resolve, Kaunteya, you will, unassailable one, kill Suyodhana with his followers.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"एवं ब्रुवति भीमं तु धर्मराजे युधिष्ठिरे ।\nआजगाम महाभागो बृहदश्वो महानृषिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Yudhishthira, king of dharma, said this to Bhima, the fortunate great sage Brihadashva arrived."}},{"n":30,"text":"तमभिप्रेक्ष्य धर्मात्मा संप्राप्तं धर्मचारिणम् ।\nशास्त्रवन्मधुपर्केण पूजयामास धर्मराट् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the dharma-practicing sage arrive, the righteous king of dharma honored him with the madhuparka as the rule requires."}},{"n":31,"text":"आश्वस्तं चैनमासीनमुपासीनो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nअभिप्रेक्ष्य महाबाहुः कृपणं बह्वभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the sage was rested and seated, Yudhishthira sat near, looked at him, and the mighty-armed one spoke at length in misery."}},{"n":32,"text":"अक्षद्यूतेन भगवन्धनं राज्यं च मे हृतम् ।\nआहूय निकृतिप्रज्ञैः कितवैरक्षकोविदैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Blessed one, my wealth and kingdom were taken at the game of dice, when gamblers who were expert at dice and cunning in fraud called me over."}},{"n":33,"text":"अनक्षज्ञस्य हि सतो निकृत्या पापनिश्चयैः ।\nभार्या च मे सभां नीता प्राणेभ्योऽपि गरीयसी ॥","meaning":{"en":"I did not know dice, and my wife, dearer than life, was taken into the assembly by those of wicked resolve with their trickery."}},{"n":34,"text":"अस्ति राजा मया कश्चिदल्पभाग्यतरो भुवि ।\nभवता दृष्टपूर्वो वा श्रुतपूर्वोऽपि वा भवेत् ।\nन मत्तो दुःखिततरः पुमानस्तीति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is there any king on earth with less fortune than I, whom you have seen or heard of? I think no man is more unhappy than I.\""}},{"text":"बृहदश्व उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brihadashva said:"}},{"n":35,"text":"यद्ब्रवीषि महाराज न मत्तो विद्यते क्वचित् ।\nअल्पभाग्यतरः कश्चित्पुमानस्तीति पाण्डव ॥","meaning":{"en":"You say, great king, that nowhere is there a man less fortunate than you, Pandava."}},{"n":36,"text":"अत्र ते कथयिष्यामि यदि शुश्रूषसेऽनघ ।\nयस्त्वत्तो दुःखिततरो राजासीत्पृथिवीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this I will tell you, if you wish to hear, blameless one: there was a king, lord of the earth, more miserable than you."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":37,"text":"अथैनमब्रवीद्राजा ब्रवीतु भगवानिति ।\nइमामवस्थां संप्राप्तं श्रोतुमिच्छामि पार्थिवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king replied, \"Let the blessed one speak. I wish to hear of the king who reached such a state.\""}},{"text":"बृहदश्व उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brihadashva said:"}},{"n":38,"text":"शृणु राजन्नवहितः सह भ्रातृभिरच्युत ।\nयस्त्वत्तो दुःखिततरो राजासीत्पृथिवीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen attentively with your brothers, Achyuta. There was a king, lord of earth, more miserable than you."}},{"n":39,"text":"निषधेषु महीपालो वीरसेन इति स्म ह ।\nतस्य पुत्रोऽभवन्नाम्ना नलो धर्मार्थदर्शिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among the Nishadhas there was a ruler named Virasena. His son was Nala, who saw clearly the aims of dharma and wealth."}},{"n":40,"text":"स निकृत्या जितो राजा पुष्करेणेति नः श्रुतम् ।\nवनवासमदुःखार्हो भार्यया न्यवसत्सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have heard that king was beaten by Pushkara through trickery, and though undeserving of suffering he lived in the forest with his wife."}},{"n":41,"text":"न तस्याश्वो न च रथो न भ्राता न च बान्धवाः ।\nवने निवसतो राजञ्शिष्यन्ते स्म कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, he had no horse, no chariot, no brother and no kinsmen left to him as he lived in the forest."}},{"n":42,"text":"भवान्हि संवृतो वीरैर्भ्रातृभिर्देवसंमितैः ।\nब्रह्मकल्पैर्द्विजाग्र्यैश्च तस्मान्नार्हसि शोचितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You, though, are surrounded by heroic brothers equal to gods and by foremost brahmins like Brahma; so you should not grieve."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":43,"text":"विस्तरेणाहमिच्छामि नलस्य सुमहात्मनः ।\nचरितं वदतां श्रेष्ठ तन्ममाख्यातुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wish to hear in detail the story of the greatly noble Nala. Best of speakers, please tell it to me."}}]}]}